{"Title":"An Act relative to reasonable municipal expenses","BillNumber":"S2143","DocketNumber":"SD1012","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T16:46:19.27"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T16:46:19.27"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2143/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Lewis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2143) of Jason M. Lewis for legislation relative to reasonable municipal expenses.  Telecommunications, Utilities and Energy.","DocumentText":"\tSection 69H of Chapter 164 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting at the end thereof the following clause:- \r\n\t“(5) the board shall consider the requests of municipalities for reimbursement of expenses spent in relation to the application and may assess fees on applicants for reasonable municipal expenses related to the application.” \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[],"Amendments":[]}